@@ -0,0 +1,14 @@
+# The Elder Scrolls V: Skyrim
+
+Switch update **1.1.404 / v393216**, SDK 14, Creation Engine over NVN. Use this update with the base game. The normal NSP build checks both `main` and `sdk` against `game.tsv`. Other builds do not inherit these settings through automatic profile derivation. `--provisional` can be used to survey an unsupported build independently.
+
+- **Shader extraction:** the matching build stores inline NVN control/code records in `main` and in a stored FXP member of `Data/Skyrim - Shaders.bsa`. The generic reader checks their descriptor ranges and shader stages. This is not a compressed-BSA reader. Shader tables are made from the user's dump under the build work directory, not shipped as source.
+- **Startup with a bounded alias window:** Default Heap and BSSmallBlockAllocator reserve 512 MiB and 256 MiB instead of 2 GiB and 1 GiB. Initial commits, GPU/File Heap reservations, stack and app pool are unchanged. These cuts work with the profile's 5.5 GiB reservation and 4.875 GiB alias region. The original layout aborts before `nnMain` in the constrained Mac test, while either half alone fails later. Reaching the frame loop does not establish long-session heap headroom.
+- **Helgen Keep brightness:** mode 7 now initializes Metal's separate stencil plane before the game's raw D24S8 compute pass. Mode 1 still clears depth only. This is the 1.1.404 site for the approach in [nxnative PR #444](https://github.com/seedds/nxnative/pull/444), not the older build's patch address. The original instructions are checked before rewriting.
+- **New Game and Quit:** bounded overlapping linear rows need a private Metal sampling copy with an in-order refresh after copy/clear writeback. The shell must also park guest threads before reclaiming the AudioOut instances that the renderer can still close.
+
+The opening cart and a Helgen checkpoint were exercised on Mac with the repair inputs. These checks do not establish physical iPhone address-space limits, sustained handheld play, or Quit-to-library and relaunch on a phone.
+
+## Experimental frame rate
+
+Mac offers 30 fps (original) and 60 fps (experimental) for the verified main and SDK. For local iPhone diagnostics only, `DM_SKYRIM_FPS_PROTOTYPE=1` at framework build time enables the same setting. Standard iPhone builds do not offer it. Unset or `DM_SKYRIM_FPS=30` preserves the game's pacing and dynamic-resolution thresholds. The 60 fps option changes present cadence and the dynamic-resolution frame budgets, not simulation timing. Movies and serious thermal state fall back to 30 fps. Physics, cinematics and sustained device performance are not qualified.
